<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Arnotts 13-month net profit A$60.9mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Arnotts 13-month net profit A$60.9mln.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to July 28, 1996</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   109.62 vs 121.17</p>
<p>    Net				     60.89 vs 53.32</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	    14.00 vs 17.00</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	    26.00 vs 32.00</p>
<p>    Sales				  729.27 vs 641.07</p>
<p>    Other income			   5.59 vs 31.00</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    43.7 vs 38.3</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		 loss 12.97 vs loss 37.03</p>
<p>    Tax				     34.82 vs 29.32</p>
<p>    Interest				 0.98 vs 1.54</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  31.03 vs 26.65</p>
<p>    Minorities			     0.94 vs 1.52</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 percent franked</p>
<p>Pay date November 15</p>
<p>Reg date October 31  </p>
<p>NOTE: Arnotts Ltd is a biscuit maker and is majority owned by Campbell Soup Co of the United States. 1996 figures are for the 13 month period to July 28 while comparative figures are for the 12 months to June 30, 1995.  </p>
<p>On a 12 month basis to June 30, sales were A$675.12 million, operating profit was A$102.42 million while net profit was A$57.39 million.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
